From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] board: odroid-go-ultra: the kernel Image at a 2 MiB boundary

meson64's kernel_addr_r is 0x08080000; booti runs an Image at a 2 MiB
boundary and moved it there first (memmove of the whole Image, 0.2 s for
the 42 MiB arm64 defconfig kernel). Load it at 0x08200000 instead,
unless the environment was changed.

diff --git a/board/amlogic/odroid-go-ultra/odroid-go-ultra.c b/board/amlogic/odroid-go-ultra/odroid-go-ultra.c
index a5b46f2ea09..03269e3ef07 100644
--- a/board/amlogic/odroid-go-ultra/odroid-go-ultra.c
+++ b/board/amlogic/odroid-go-ultra/odroid-go-ultra.c
@@ -243,6 +243,12 @@ int meson_board_late_init(void)
 {
 	ogu_charge_wait();
 	ogu_ums_key();
+	/*
+	 * The kernel Image where booti runs it: at meson64's 0x08080000
+	 * booti first moves it to the next 2 MiB boundary (tens of MiB).
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(env_get("kernel_addr_r") ?: "", "0x08080000"))
+		env_set("kernel_addr_r", "0x08200000");
 	return 0;
 }
 
